  "case": {
    "annotations": {
      "notes": [
        "The callee rejects the INVITE (600) while the caller's PRACK to its reliable 183 is unanswered; the PRACK server transaction outlives the INVITE's final (RFC 3261 §17.2.2), so the callee still owes it a final (§8.2.6) and answers 200 after the ACK.",
        "The system answers the caller's PRACK 200 itself once the callee leg is torn down. The document names 481 to the PRACK, the answer another implementation gave: one status substitution on the PRACK step, charged to the transaction it rides (§17.1.3), whichever order the 600 and the 200 leave in.",
        "The 481 expect is retired by the 200 (a final ends its transaction), the scripted ACK to the 600 follows, and the flow runs to its end."
      ]
    },
    "family": "transparent",
    "id": "answer-on-the-other-transaction",
    "lanes": {
      "upstream-fake": "ok"
    },
    "origin": "authored",
    "title": "a response no expect matched is charged to the expect of its own transaction",
    "variant": "repro"
  },
